# IRESI platform environment.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill it in. `.env.local` is gitignored and
# must stay that way — it holds a database password.
#
# THE PUBLIC SITE NEEDS NONE OF THIS. With every value unset, all public pages
# still build and render: the database-backed lists show their empty states and
# the contact form stores messages instead of emailing them. Only the admin
# needs a database.

# Which project this deployment serves: `iresi` or `adflex`.
#
# Unset means `iresi`. An unrecognised value fails at startup rather than
# quietly serving the wrong project's name, navigation and contact address.
ACTIVE_PROJECT=iresi

# Postgres connection string. Use the POOLED string on Neon or Supabase — the
# direct one opens a connection per instance and exhausts the limit under load.
#
#   Local: postgresql://postgres:password@localhost:5432/iresi
DATABASE_URL=

# Signs the admin session cookie. At least 32 characters.
#
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
#
# Changing this signs everyone out immediately, which is also how to revoke
# every session at once if a laptop goes missing.
SESSION_SECRET=

# The public address of the site, with scheme and no trailing path.
#
# NOT SET YET, AND DELIBERATELY NOT GUESSED. Where this will be staged has not
# been confirmed — item 1.4 on the access list. Until it is set the site omits
# everything that needs an absolute URL: no canonical link, no Open Graph URL,
# an empty sitemap. A wrong value is worse than none, because a canonical
# pointing at a domain that does not exist tells search engines the real page is
# somewhere else.
#
# READ AT BUILD TIME, not at request time. Changing it needs a rebuild;
# restarting the server picks up nothing.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contact form email
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ONLY THE PASSWORD LIVES HERE. The sending mailbox, mail server and port are
# set in `MAIL_SENDER` in src/lib/site.ts, and the address enquiries arrive at
# comes from the active project's config. The password is the exception because
# this file is gitignored, and a credential in a source file is a credential in
# the git history for good.
#
# Gmail and Microsoft 365 both reject the ordinary account password over SMTP.
# This has to be an app password, or an account with SMTP AUTH switched on.
#
# While it is empty the site cannot send, and every contact form message goes to
# the admin dashboard instead. Nothing breaks and nothing is lost.
SMTP_PASSWORD=
